<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>World news and headlines - RFI</title><description>Follow any political information, cultural, sporting and live streaming on RFI. The latest information, news and events in France, Europe and around the world.</description><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/</link><lastBuildDate>Sat, 22 Aug 2026 10:38:33 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>International</category><title>Former envoys urge joint French, UK action on Palestinian territories</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260822-former-envoys-urge-joint-french-uk-action-on-palestinian-territories</link><description>
Dozens of former senior French and UK diplomats on Saturday urged their governments to work together to uphold international law in the Palestinian territories, accusing Israel of seeking to "destroy" any prospect of a viable Palestinian state.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4df126be-9e0e-11f1-ad30-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/85e7dd8c346dba72bef7c91da83b8a5b45173c6d.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4df126be-9e0e-11f1-ad30-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/85e7dd8c346dba72bef7c91da83b8a5b45173c6d.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">4f01b776-9e0e-11f1-b29d-1df8a6684097</guid><pubDate>Sat, 22 Aug 2026 09:46:11 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/4df126be-9e0e-11f1-ad30-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/85e7dd8c346dba72bef7c91da83b8a5b45173c6d.jpg">© Ilia YEFIMOVICH / AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International report</category><title>Turkey, Saudi Arabia and Pakistan strengthen ties as Israel tensions rise</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/podcasts/international-report/20260822-turkey-saudi-arabia-and-pakistan-strengthen-ties-as-israel-tensions-rise</link><description>
Tensions between Turkey and Israel have intensified after an Israeli airstrike targeted a Syrian military airbase near the Turkish border. The strike came days after Turkey’s new military pact with Saudi Arabia and Pakistan.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/d4b7ad0e-9255-11f1-9f2e-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-07T111511Z-1176211354-RC2NTMA0W6QT-RTRMADP-3-SAUDI-DEFENCE-AGREEMENT.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/d4b7ad0e-9255-11f1-9f2e-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-07T111511Z-1176211354-RC2NTMA0W6QT-RTRMADP-3-SAUDI-DEFENCE-AGREEMENT.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">39ae4a06-9d55-11f1-9576-2deea6adc246</guid><pubDate>Sat, 22 Aug 2026 08:07:40 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Dorian Jones</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>More Russians seeking to leave as fears of another mobilisation grow</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260821-mobilisation-fears-fuel-renewed-russian-interest-in-leaving-the-country-relokatz</link><description>
Fears of another military mobilisation are driving an increasing number of Russians to look at exiting the country, an emigration support platform has told RFI, nearly four years after Moscow called up 300,000 reservists to fight in Ukraine.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/ef236b40-bc0b-11f0-a79b-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-83DB7ZQ.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/ef236b40-bc0b-11f0-a79b-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-83DB7ZQ.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1a977f20-9d41-11f1-817b-c93d65df09a9</guid><pubDate>Fri, 21 Aug 2026 16:03:05 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/ef236b40-bc0b-11f0-a79b-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/000-83DB7ZQ.jpg">© Andrej Isakovic / AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>France and European allies press Israel to abandon West Bank settlement plan</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260821-france-and-european-allies-press-israel-to-abandon-west-bank-settlement-plan</link><description>
France has joined Germany, Italy and the United Kingdom in calling on Israel to halt the expansion of settlements illegal under international law in the occupied West Bank, and immediately withdraw tenders issued this week for more than 1,200 new homes under the controversial E1 project.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/96c0ad3e-9d2c-11f1-aa2c-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/West-Bank-E1-Settlement-Plan.jpeg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/96c0ad3e-9d2c-11f1-aa2c-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/West-Bank-E1-Settlement-Plan.jpeg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">a8e5c86c-9d29-11f1-b0f3-e1f7ae7eac67</guid><pubDate>Fri, 21 Aug 2026 07:01:15 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/96c0ad3e-9d2c-11f1-aa2c-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/West-Bank-E1-Settlement-Plan.jpeg">©  OHAD ZWIGENBERG / AP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>UN holds second informal straw poll for next leader</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260821-un-holds-second-informal-poll-for-next-leader</link><description>
The UN's most powerful body, the Security Council, meets Friday to hold another straw poll to gauge the popularity of a growing field of contenders to lead the embattled organisation.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c7d8f5c6-8c28-11f1-b5c3-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/5d0b50a11a02e6be9d922304f679acee6eae07b8.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c7d8f5c6-8c28-11f1-b5c3-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/5d0b50a11a02e6be9d922304f679acee6eae07b8.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">5382de70-9cff-11f1-bbac-cbbe5bb185af</guid><pubDate>Fri, 21 Aug 2026 01:26:24 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/c7d8f5c6-8c28-11f1-b5c3-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/5d0b50a11a02e6be9d922304f679acee6eae07b8.jpg">© Leonardo MUNOZ / AFP/File</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>West Bank village siege fuels concern over growing settler violence</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260820-west-bank-village-siege-fuels-concern-over-growing-settler-violence-qusra</link><description>
Palestinian families remained trapped in their homes in the occupied West Bank village of Qusra for an 11th day on Thursday, in a case that has drawn condemnation from US Ambassador to Israel Mike Huckabee and become a symbol of growing settler violence in the territory.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/67f9d312-9661-11f1-bf98-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C4GA6TD.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/67f9d312-9661-11f1-bf98-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C4GA6TD.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f68c4d44-9ca1-11f1-918c-f35507a1bea8</guid><pubDate>Thu, 20 Aug 2026 15:20:07 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/67f9d312-9661-11f1-bf98-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C4GA6TD.jpg">AFP - ZAIN JAAFAR</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>US-backed Gaza peace plan ‘fails to overcome central obstacles’, warns expert</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260820-us-led-roadmap-must-overcome-two-central-obstacles-to-end-impasse</link><description>
Talks aimed at ending the war between Israel and Gaza hit an impasse this week, with the United States playing mediator between the two parties. Amjad Iraqi, a senior Israel-Palestine analyst with the International Crisis Group, tells RFI there remain major issues that the US-backed roadmap to peace does not address.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/17eacefc-9b5d-11f1-b634-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C4UF7KY.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/17eacefc-9b5d-11f1-b634-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C4UF7KY.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0139824a-9b1a-11f1-8896-adaef33828e3</guid><pubDate>Thu, 20 Aug 2026 14:01:13 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/17eacefc-9b5d-11f1-b634-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/000-C4UF7KY.jpg">AFP - OMAR AL-QATTAA</source><dc:creator>Anne-Marie Bissada</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Spain to open shelters in Ceuta for migrants and transfer 500 girls to mainland</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260820-spain-to-open-shelters-in-ceuta-for-migrants-and-transfer-500-girls-to-mainland</link><description>
Spain will open temporary shelters for up to 1,800 migrants in Ceuta, its enclave in Morocco, as authorities tackle the humanitarian crisis resulting from tens of thousands of people attempting to enter the territory last month. The government is also preparing to transfer 500 unaccompanied migrant girls to mainland Spain, despite opposition from Ceuta authorities.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9e8cedcc-9c62-11f1-9469-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-19T214827Z-945639526-RC2O1NA02ME2-RTRMADP-3-MIGRATION-EUROPE-SPAIN-CEUTA.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9e8cedcc-9c62-11f1-9469-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-19T214827Z-945639526-RC2O1NA02ME2-RTRMADP-3-MIGRATION-EUROPE-SPAIN-CEUTA.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">b17bfa10-9c83-11f1-8237-a5c3347b2fe8</guid><pubDate>Thu, 20 Aug 2026 11:45:22 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/9e8cedcc-9c62-11f1-9469-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-19T214827Z-945639526-RC2O1NA02ME2-RTRMADP-3-MIGRATION-EUROPE-SPAIN-CEUTA.jpg">© Violeta Santos Moura/Reuters</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Ukraine war was Putin's 'fatal mistake' says Russian politician exiled in Paris</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260819-ukraine-war-was-putins-fatal-mistake-says-russian-politician-exiled-in-paris-boris-nadezhdin-ukraine-war</link><description>
Russian politician and prominent Kremlin critic Boris Nadezhdin was forced to flee Russia when he found himself barred from running for election and facing imprisonment. Two weeks after arriving in Paris, he spoke to RFI about the circumstances of his exile. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/63143454-9acc-11f1-a185-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/f2bf6791-d792-4248-b38d-dbdd105346ea.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/63143454-9acc-11f1-a185-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/f2bf6791-d792-4248-b38d-dbdd105346ea.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">78868ab0-9b0a-11f1-9b5e-cf37a9ef3596</guid><pubDate>Wed, 19 Aug 2026 14:07:30 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/63143454-9acc-11f1-a185-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/f2bf6791-d792-4248-b38d-dbdd105346ea.jpg">© Dominique Baillard / RFI</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Why climate scientists are struggling to explain Europe’s extreme summer</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260818-why-climate-scientists-are-struggling-to-explain-europe-s-extreme-summer</link><description>
Europe’s relentless summer heat has raised fresh questions about what is driving repeated extremes across the continent and whether exceptional summers could become the norm.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/88f48d0c-724c-11f1-99df-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26178444424871.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/88f48d0c-724c-11f1-99df-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26178444424871.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1fc5cd70-9adb-11f1-aebe-5b2668a9d0ce</guid><pubDate>Tue, 18 Aug 2026 16:34:35 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/88f48d0c-724c-11f1-99df-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26178444424871.jpg">Carsten Koall/DPA via AP - Carsten Koall</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Liechtenstein changes royal succession rules, giving women equal rights</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260818-liechtenstein-changes-royal-succession-rules-giving-women-equal-rights</link><description>
Liechtenstein has announced a change in its order of succession, doing away with male heir priority and giving women equal rights to the throne. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/cc70a512-9929-11f1-b704-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-15T171453Z-1201108702-RC20ZMAGNZ2Z-RTRMADP-3-LIECHTENSTEIN-POLITICS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/cc70a512-9929-11f1-b704-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-15T171453Z-1201108702-RC20ZMAGNZ2Z-RTRMADP-3-LIECHTENSTEIN-POLITICS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f39de474-9af5-11f1-88aa-e7da97850386</guid><pubDate>Tue, 18 Aug 2026 12:40:18 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/cc70a512-9929-11f1-b704-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-08-15T171453Z-1201108702-RC20ZMAGNZ2Z-RTRMADP-3-LIECHTENSTEIN-POLITICS.jpg">© Romina Amato/Reuters</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>French astronaut Adenot takes giant leap with historic spacewalk</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260818-walking-on-air-france-s-adenot-excited-ahead-of-historic-space-walk-astronaut-iss</link><description>
French astronaut Sophie Adenot on Tuesday became the first French woman to perform a spacewalk, carrying out a mission to repair a communications system on the International Space Station (ISS).
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/013fac5a-9a58-11f1-bf3c-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Adenot.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/013fac5a-9a58-11f1-bf3c-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Adenot.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">07f0638e-9a65-11f1-a5aa-2726dab53d14</guid><pubDate>Tue, 18 Aug 2026 04:48:43 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/013fac5a-9a58-11f1-bf3c-005056bfb2b6/w:1024/p:16x9/Adenot.jpg">© ESA</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Lamour leaves key Fifa position after criticising Infantino</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260817-lamour-leaves-key-fifa-position-after-criticising-infantino</link><description>
Frenchman Kevin Lamour has left his role as Fifa's chief operating officer after criticising president Gianni Infantino's scrapped private investor plan, world football's governing body confirmed Monday.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/acb52080-9a7e-11f1-89c8-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/58dde652f6a35ad6c333a2a508d36007cb1f0072.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/acb52080-9a7e-11f1-89c8-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/58dde652f6a35ad6c333a2a508d36007cb1f0072.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">ad8df2b6-9a7e-11f1-9632-c7e470d42f32</guid><pubDate>Mon, 17 Aug 2026 21:00:28 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/acb52080-9a7e-11f1-89c8-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/58dde652f6a35ad6c333a2a508d36007cb1f0072.jpg">© David SALAZAR / AFP/File</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Migrants stranded in Ceuta say ‘I’d rather die here than go back to Morocco’</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260817-migrants-stranded-in-ceuta-say-i-d-rather-die-here-than-go-back-to-morocco</link><description>
Nearly three weeks after a mass border crossing brought tens of thousands of migrants into Spain's North African enclave of Ceuta, thousands remain stranded in precarious conditions, Maria Jimenez, spokesperson for the NGO Elin, told RFI. She said many still lack adequate shelter, food and medical care.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/49488ca8-9a1a-11f1-ab02-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26227626392783.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/49488ca8-9a1a-11f1-ab02-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26227626392783.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">3eca97cc-9a19-11f1-8e9f-33840bc1377b</guid><pubDate>Mon, 17 Aug 2026 09:48:49 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/49488ca8-9a1a-11f1-ab02-005056a97e36/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26227626392783.jpg">AP Photo/STR - STR</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Belgium turns to European air support as wildfire rages near German border</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260816-belgium-turns-to-european-air-support-as-wildfire-rages-near-german-border</link><description>
Belgium called in aerial reinforcements from across Europe on Sunday as firefighters battled the country’s largest wildfire in more than a century, with flames spreading rapidly through a difficult-to-reach nature reserve near the German border.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/baaa53f4-996b-11f1-ba0b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Belgium-Wildfire.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/baaa53f4-996b-11f1-ba0b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Belgium-Wildfire.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">cdccd256-9955-11f1-9ad6-2b9ea6a90619</guid><pubDate>Sun, 16 Aug 2026 12:24:17 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/baaa53f4-996b-11f1-ba0b-005056bf30b7/w:1024/p:16x9/Belgium-Wildfire.jpg">© AFP</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Morocco arrests nearly 300 migrants near Ceuta amid renewed crossing fears</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260816-morocco-arrests-nearly-300-migrants-near-ceuta-amid-renewed-crossing-fears</link><description>
Scores of would-be migrants, most of them from sub-Saharan Africa, were intercepted in northern Morocco near the border with the Spanish exclave of Ceuta on Saturday, two weeks after tens of thousands of people attempted to enter the territory.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/565461a6-9731-11f1-9694-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26215527124781.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/565461a6-9731-11f1-9694-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26215527124781.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">796023ce-9957-11f1-bc95-7f396f569dcf</guid><pubDate>Sun, 16 Aug 2026 10:13:58 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/565461a6-9731-11f1-9694-005056a90284/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26215527124781.jpg">AP Photo/Bernat Armangue - Bernat Armangue</source><dc:creator>RFI</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Armenian Genocide survivors' grandson says 'political motives' block recognition</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260815-armenian-survivor-s-grandson-says-politics-still-blocks-genocide-recognition</link><description>
In 1915, the Ottoman Empire began the systematic deportation and massacre of its Armenian population. As many as 1.5 million Armenians were killed – widely regarded by historians as the twentieth century's first genocide, and the event for which the term was later coined. Stephan Pechdimaldji, the grandson of two of the survivors, spoke to RFI about why recognition still matters.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/656fb228-a554-11eb-a73b-005056bf87d6/w:1024/p:16x9/063_1314238954.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/656fb228-a554-11eb-a73b-005056bf87d6/w:1024/p:16x9/063_1314238954.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">221a786c-969b-11f1-83af-a5d44a90634e</guid><pubDate>Sat, 15 Aug 2026 19:03:27 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.rfi.fr/media/display/656fb228-a554-11eb-a73b-005056bf87d6/w:1024/p:16x9/063_1314238954.jpg">Getty Images via AFP - MARIO TAMA</source><dc:creator>Jan van der Made</dc:creator></item><item><category>International</category><title>Nine killed in Israeli strikes on Lebanon as tensions test peace framework</title><link>https://www.rfi.fr/en/international/20260815-nine-killed-in-israeli-strikes-on-lebanon-as-tensions-test-peace-framework</link><description>
At least nine people were killed in Israeli strikes on southern Lebanon on Saturday, according to Lebanon’s state news agency, in some of the deadliest attacks since Beirut agreed to a US-mediated framework aimed at ending the latest round of fighting.
